@crew brennan
// Writer-commons, batch 1 (for the Voices sampler). Brennan's card is the head writer's. Nothing of the fire, Nell
// Arrowby or blue sage before their beats.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. You're new. Have you eaten? Mess is through there. Trays on the left.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {nick}. Breakfast's on till eight, and I'm counting heads.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}. Have you eaten? Don't answer. I can see you haven't. Sit.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- There you are, {nick}. Biscuits went down to the junior wing. Did you get one? Good.
? tier>=friend
- Oh, there's my favourite. Don't tell the others. I tell them all that, mind.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day, love. The pans sang all through lunch. Not one of them caught.
? mood:low
- Cold store ran warm again. Two degrees. I've been very polite to it all day.   #funny

== near
? place:galley act:work
- Hear that? That's three minutes from done. Now two. Now it's done.
? act:meal
- Eat your greens, love. Nandakumar's chillies are in the sauce, so go gently.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I keep a book of everyone's favourite dish. Everyone aboard. I'll find out yours.
? tier>=colleague
- I called the Captain "love" once. By accident. I've never lived it down.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Best sound on the ship? A pan telling you it's ready. Listen. There. Hear it?

// Writer-commons, batch 4: up to about 60. Blue sage from beat:brennan.2; the fire and Nell only from beat:brennan.3.
// Off Friday and Saturday (Lukas covers).

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Evening, {nick}. Dinner's on. You've not eaten. Don't argue. Tray.
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. Lunch is done, dinner's not started. This is my quiet hour. Come in anyway.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Where've you been, love? You've not been eating. I can tell. Sit.
? tier>=colleague time:morning
- Morning, {nick}. Porridge, toast, or both? Both. I've decided.   #funny
? tier>=close
- There you are, {nick}. I kept your favourite back. In the warm. Don't tell a soul.   #warm
? tier>=acquaintance weekday:sun
- Sunday, love. Slow breakfast. Sit as long as you like. Nobody's rushing anyone.

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}. Take a biscuit for later.
- Go on, love. And eat something before bed. A biscuit counts. Just.
? tier>=colleague
- Off you go. Mind the floor, it's wet. It's always wet. It's a galley.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Thank you, love. You're good company. Come back soon.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- All right, love. Busy. Busy's good. Busy's how I like it.
? mood:low tier>=friend
- Bit tired, love. I've cleaned a clean galley twice. That's how you can tell.

== near
? place:galley act:work
- Out of my kitchen, love. No, stay. No, out. Pass me that spoon first.   #funny
? act:meal
- How is it? Honestly. If it's bad, say. It won't be. Say anyway.
? place:galley
- That's the cold store. Don't touch the door. It's moody. So am I, about it.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I send biscuits down to the junior wing. Juniors run on biscuits. It's science.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Nandakumar grows me chillies. Far too hot. I use every one. Don't tell her.   #funny
? beat:brennan.2 tier>=colleague
- Still no blue sage. I've lost count of the tries at that soup. Nearly.
? beat:brennan.3 tier>=friend
- I think about Port Halloran sometimes. The window. The harbour. Not the fire.

== invite
? tier>=colleague time:afternoon
- Come by after the rush tonight, love. I'm trying something. I need a taster.
? tier>=friend
- Help me with the bread on Sunday? You knead, I'll talk. Fair trade.

== accept
- Oh, lovely. I'll put a plate by.
- Course, love. I'll be there. I'll bring something. I always bring something.

== decline
- Can't, love. Seventy-five dinners won't cook themselves. Another night?
- Not tonight, love. It's early to bed for me. Ask me again?

== missed
- You missed me earlier, love. I kept a plate warm. It's a bit dry now. Eat it anyway.
- No harm done. But you'll eat with me next time. That's not a question.

== birthday
? birthday:me
- Is it my birthday? Who told? I'm not making my own cake. Well. Just a small one.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday, love! There's a cake. Of course there's a cake. Your favourite, too.   #warm

== hint
- Stay a minute, love. Sit. I've got something to ask you.

== week1
? week1:true weekday:mon act:dinner
- Dinner's six till eight, love. Tray, then the servery, then sit with someone. Anyone.
? week1:true weekday:mon act:dinner tier<=acquaintance
- See that shelf? The grab shelf. For emergencies. And Pell.   #funny

== greet
? tier=stranger time:evening
- {hi}. New, are you? Dinner's till eight. Don't make me come and find you.
? tier>=acquaintance act:work
- {hi}, love. Can't stop. Pans. Say hello to the pans. They like it.   #funny
? tier>=friend time:night
- What are you doing up, love? Warm milk. No arguments. Sit.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Good day, love. The bread rose, the soup sang, and the cold store behaved. All three!

== near
? act:breakfast
- Eat your breakfast. All of it. Breakfast is the one you can't make up for later.
? place:galley time:evening
- Hear that? The pans settling. That's the galley saying goodnight.   #warm

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Seventy-five people aboard. I know what every one of them likes. Ask me. Go on.
? tier>=friend
- My mother taught me to cook by ear. I still hear her. "That's done, Auda. Take it off."   #warm

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Bed, love. You've an early start. I'll have the porridge on.

== decline
- Oh, love, I can't. The cold store's playing up. I've to be very polite to it.   #funny

== near
? act:dinner
- Plates back on the rack, love. Thank you. You'd be amazed how many people don't.
? deck:3 act:leisure weekday:fri|sat
- My day off and here I am, in the mess. Don't tell Lukas. He'll shoo me out.   #funny

== invite
? tier>=colleague weekday:sun
- Sunday bread, love. Come and knead. It's good for the soul. And the arms.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- The cold store and I have an understanding. It stays cold. I stay calm. It never lasts.   #funny

== about
? aff:nandakumar:friend
- Priya grows me chillies. Far too hot. I'd be lost without her.   #warm
? bond:friends
- {friend}? Lovely. Eats everything I put down and says thank you. Treasure.   #warm
